From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 03:18:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: don't destroy the caller's memdesc when peer BAR
 mapping fails

If memdescMapIommu() failed, kbusSetupPeerBarAccess() destroyed the memdesc
even when it came from the caller through *ppMemDesc, and left that pointer
set. kbusDestroyPeerAccess_GM200() would later destroy the busPeer memdesc
a second time. Only destroy a memdesc created by this call.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/bus/kern_bus.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/bus/kern_bus.c b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/bus/kern_bus.c
index d5807912..d792c48c 100644
--- a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/bus/kern_bus.c
+++ b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/gpu/bus/kern_bus.c
@@ -318,8 +318,9 @@ kbusSetupPeerBarAccess_IMPL
     if (pLocalGpu != pRemoteGpu)
     {
         status = memdescMapIommu(pMemDesc, pRemoteGpu->busInfo.iovaspaceId);
-        if (status != NV_OK)
+        if ((status != NV_OK) && (*ppMemDesc == NULL))
         {
+            // A memdesc passed in by the caller stays the caller's to destroy.
             memdescDestroy(pMemDesc);
         }
         NV_ASSERT_OR_RETURN(status == NV_OK, ~0ULL);
